      "content": "the \"debris holding unit\" idea is actually pretty smart, i might try that. it's just that even with the holding unit, it's the sheer *nature* of these things that's getting to me. they're so small, so tiny, and they always seem to be in the exact worst spots—wedged deep in a fold, or tucked into a seam where you almost miss them. \n\nit's almost like they're these little, pesky, uninvited guests that have made themselves at home in the shadows of the collection. it's not just clutter; it's like this constant, tiny, irritating presence that's just... there, waiting to trip you up. does that kind of thing ever happen in other archives, where the mess feels less like passive dirt and more like a bunch of little, troublesome things just trying to mess with the order?",
